BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Saturday Movie: The Girl Who Cried Pearls and Higglety Piggley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T160000
UID:6a21a73a46d5f64f7dcdeff6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In Montreal\, at the dawn of the 20th century\, a poor boy fal
 ls in love with a girl whose sorrow turns into pearls. He sells them to a 
 ruthless pawnbroker\, who hungers for more. Tempted by greed\, the boy mus
 t choose between love and fortune. The choice could damn his soul.\nThe 20
 26 Oscar® Winner for Best Animated Short Film from the acclaimed team of
  Chris Lavis and Maciek Szczerbowski. This meticulously crafted film is a
  testament to the magic of stop-motion animation. With handmade puppets\, 
 mesmerizing narration by Colm Feore and a haunting score by Patrick Watson
 \,\nThe Girl Who Cried Pearls\nis a timeless parable of desire\, deception
  and the price of innocence.\nAlso screening from the same Oscar winning t
 eam with be\nHigglety Pigglety Pop! or There Must Be More to Life\n. This 
 live-action/animated adaptation of Maurice Sendak's book features the voic
 es of Meryl Streep and Forest Whitaker.\nThe story follows Jennie the ter
 rier's suspenseful and unexpectedly moving journey to gain new experience
 s and realize her dream of becoming the star of the World Mother Goose The
 atre.\nFilms courtesy of the National Film Board of Canada (NFB).\nDrop-in
 ! No registration required.
LOCATION:Hillcrest\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a21a73a46d5f64f7dcdeff6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
