BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wonder Workshop: Introduction to Design Thinking Building Challeng
 e
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260721T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260721T153000
UID:6a11e856caf93436005de0d1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered what it would be like to be an inventor
 ?\nHave you ever thought about building something yourself?\nWhat is somet
 hing you would like to build?\nIs there a problem you would like to fix?\n
 Use your imagination and brainstorm creative solutions to develop a machin
 e that will fix a problem or make a task easier for you!\nPlus\, enter a p
 rize draw for a chance to win an awesome book. For kids ages 4 to 8 with 
 their parents/caregivers.
LOCATION:Humber Summit - Closed\, Auditorium\, Lower level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a11e856caf93436005de0d1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mr. Eric's Musical Adventures
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T111500
UID:6a11f23c8e677a28001e116d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Mr. Eric's Musical Adventures is a music lesson packaged in si
 lly fun and nonsense! Through highly engaging and catchy original songs an
 d interactive audience participation\, Mr. Eric teaches rhythm\, rhyming\,
  song writing\, singing\, movement\, and pitch\, with a big boost of vocab
 ulary to boot! While he’s spent years as a professional orchestra conduc
 tor\, Mr. Eric has found a special kind of joy in sharing music and storie
 s with young audiences!\nFor children ages 4-8. Drop in.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a11f23c8e677a28001e116d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
